Fabrikam, Inc. partitions an Orders table by OrderDate. Each boundary date must be the lower limit of its partition. How should you complete the code? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.

```sql
CREATE PARTITION FUNCTION pfOrders (DATE)
AS RANGE [[1]]
FOR VALUES ('2025-01-01', '2025-02-01');

CREATE PARTITION SCHEME psOrders
AS PARTITION pfOrders ALL TO ([PRIMARY]);

CREATE TABLE dbo.Orders (
    OrderId INT NOT NULL,
    OrderDate DATE NOT NULL
) ON psOrders ([[2]]);
```
